<title>USA: GM January U.S. vehicle sales off 0.9 pct.</title>
<headline>GM January U.S. vehicle sales off 0.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Corp</p>
<p>			Jan 1-31, 1997     Jan 1-31, 1996 *Pct Chng</p>
<p> Total Car		190,742	   183,481	     +4.0</p>
<p> Total Truck	    141,258	   151,477	     -6.7</p>
<p> Total Vehicle	  332,000	   334,958	     -0.9</p>
<p>* Pct change based on daily selling rate. Sale days 26 in latest month vs 26 in year-ago period.</p>
<p>Total car sales figures include U.S. sales results from Saab Automobile AB, which is 50 percent-owned by GM and Sweden's AB Investor Saab's U.S. sales in January were 1,361 cars vs 1,558 cars a year earlier.</p>
</text>
